  "worked_solution": "First, we write down the coordinates of the images relative to the basis $B:$\n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, the $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $B.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=2,$ $b=1,$ $c=1$ and \n\n$$\na+b+c=2+1+1=4.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
